{"task":"transcribe","language":"english","duration":46.66999816894531,"text":"Above Amphisa, on the hill of the ancient Acropolis, stands a castle that reads like a book if you look at it from the bottom up. At its base are enormous ancient blocks, worked so that they lock together without mortar, like a puzzle. On top of them sit medieval walls of smaller stones and lime, and higher still, towers built by Frankish lords in the 13th century. Nobody pulled down what came before in order to build their own. Each of them stood on what they found. Below spreads the Valley of Olive Trees, one of the largest in Greece, with trees that are themselves hundreds of years old. The ancient blocks at the base are cut so precisely that you cannot slide paper between them, and they hold with nothing sticking them together.","words":[{"word":"Above","start":0,"end":0.8799999952316284},{"word":"Amphisa","start":0.8799999952316284,"end":1.440000057220459},{"word":"on","start":1.7999999523162842,"end":2},{"word":"the","start":2,"end":2.3399999141693115},{"word":"hill","start":2.3399999141693115,"end":2.4000000953674316},{"word":"of","start":2.4000000953674316,"end":2.640000104904175},{"word":"the","start":2.640000104904175,"end":2.799999952316284},{"word":"ancient","start":2.799999952316284,"end":3.0999999046325684},{"word":"Acropolis","start":3.0999999046325684,"end":3.559999942779541},{"word":"stands","start":4.28000020980835,"end":4.460000038146973},{"word":"a","start":4.460000038146973,"end":5.059999942779541},{"word":"castle","start":5.059999942779541,"end":5.059999942779541},{"word":"that","start":5.059999942779541,"end":5.539999961853027},{"word":"reads","start":5.539999961853027,"end":5.860000133514404},{"word":"like","start":5.860000133514404,"end":6.119999885559082},{"word":"a","start":6.119999885559082,"end":6.539999961853027},{"word":"book","start":6.539999961853027,"end":6.559999942779541},{"word":"if","start":6.559999942779541,"end":6.840000152587891},{"word":"you","sta